    "summary": "Fresh plan-only ACCEPT after transition-0020. IA-18.4-BOOTSTRAP-01 is resolved: authorization-only October Web starts with ordinary Identity/management authority and allowlists, exposes only grant issuance/validation, and never opens or migrates an October target. Generator prepare validates the live grant and connected identity before its sole authorized migration and atomic first-batch setup; it does not require BindAsync or a preseeded batch. Generator select and selected-data Web bind only an existing exact batch. Failed authorization leaves a fresh target empty, and the quickstart requires this fresh-empty and negative qualification. Prior plan findings P-18.4-01..04 remain resolved; integrated Story 18.1 approval, issuer, verifier, context and three closed functions remain unchanged. Architecture classification remains justified. This correction narrows mode availability and makes first-batch sequencing reachable within the user's already approved four-route, prepare/select and ordinary-startup-isolation scope; it adds no new Worker tool, Scan strategy or PRD change and does not require a fresh planned-change authorization on semantic scope. Deterministic plan-content and workflow validation returned no errors. Corrected hashes require downstream task reconciliation and complete-definition review; this verdict grants no implementation or resource approval."
